# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
# Hand the panel backlight to the session user.
#
# The panel is a single led-backlight device whose attributes are root-only by
# default: the distribution's rules tag it with "seat" but not "uaccess", and
# desktop users are not in the video group. sysfs carries no extended
# attributes either — setfacl fails with "Operation not supported" — so neither
# uaccess nor a seat-based ACL can ever grant access here; the mode is the only
# lever.
#
# Without write access the desktop gets no brightness control at all. GNOME's
# shell writes the attribute directly (MetaBacklightSysfs), falls back to
# logind's SetBrightness when that write fails, and logind refuses while the
# session is not yet foreground ("Session is not in foreground"). The failure is
# cached for the rest of the session, so the quick-settings brightness slider
# never appears.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="backlight", GROUP="users", MODE="0664"
